'''Thammaron's sceptre''' is a [[powered staff]] requiring 60 [[Magic]] to wield, available as a drop from [[revenants]]. Like most powered staves, it is only tradeable when it is fully uncharged. It was once owned by [[Thammaron]], a Tsutsaroth [[demon]] who was one of [[Zamorak]]'s most trusted allies during the reign of [[Zaros]], and later one of his key generals during the [[God Wars]]. This item counts as a [[Zamorak]]ian item in the [[God Wars Dungeon]].

The sceptre shares the same magic attack bonus as the [[trident of the seas]], and has a powerful [[passive effect]] within the [[Wilderness]] when charged with [[revenant ether]]. In addition, unlike other powered staves, the sceptre can attack players outside of [[minigames]]. The sceptre also has a "Swap" option that allows players to switch it to [[Thammaron's sceptre (a)]], which is a variant that can [[autocast]] offensive [[combat spells]] from the [[standard spellbook]] (including [[Flames of Zamorak]]) and the [[Ancient Magicks]].

The sceptre can be upgraded to an [[accursed sceptre]] by attaching the [[skull of Vet'ion]] to it, requiring level 85 Crafting or paying [[Phabelle Bile]] {{NoCoins|500000|c}}. Players can also dismantle an uncharged sceptre to receive 7,500 [[revenant ether]], resulting in {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Revenant ether|7500}}|c}} and a {{#ifexpr:{{#vardefineecho:profit|{{GEP|Revenant ether|7500}}-{{GEP|Thammaron's sceptre (u)}}}} > 0 |profit|loss}} of {{NoCoins|{{#var:profit}}|c}}.

