==Charging==
To use the sceptre's magic spell or passive effect, it must be charged with [[revenant ether]], holding up to 17,000 charges when fully charged. The first 1,000 ether (costing {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Revenant ether|1000}}|c}}) act as an activation deposit before the built-in spell or passive effect can be used. Players can configure the charges while the weapon is in their bank by right-clicking on Configure-Charges, as long as players have the required materials. The built-in spell and passive effect consume 1 charge, and will only consume from charges '''beyond''' the first 1,000 ether. There is no additional cost for using the built-in spell and activating the passive effect at the same time. Using the ''Check'' option on the sceptre will display the amount of usable charges remaining, not including the activation deposit, up to the usable limit of 16,000.

The hourly cost of constantly using this weapon's built-in spell is 1,500 ether ({{NoCoins|{{GEP|Revenant ether|1500}}|c}}). The hourly cost of casting other spells is 1,200 ether ({{NoCoins|{{GEP|Revenant ether|1200}}|c}}), as spells can only be cast every 5 [[game tick]]s.

The ether can be safely removed (including the activation deposit) by selecting the right-click ''Uncharge'' option on the sceptre, after which the sceptre becomes tradeable again.

==Passive effect==
When Thammaron's sceptre is charged, an additional 50% magic accuracy and damage boost is applied when attacking any [[NPC]] in the [[Wilderness]], consuming 1 ether per attack whether the player hits or not. It is also applied to any [[combat spells]] cast when it is equipped, though it cannot [[autocast]] them when using the staff's built in spell.

This effect will stack with a [[slayer helmet (i)]] or a [[Salve amulet(i)]] and their variants, but not both simultaneously. This makes the sceptre the second best magic weapon in the Wilderness after the [[accursed sceptre]], surpassing the damage output of a [[trident of the seas]] or [[Trident of the Swamp|swamp]] with the additional capability of attacking any hostile players, something which both tridents are incapable of doing.

==Death==
Upon [[death]] within the Wilderness, any revenant ether stored within the sceptre will '''always''' be dropped, even if the sceptre is one of the player's protected items. Because of this, despite the sceptre being able to store a maximum of 17,000 revenant ether, it is recommended to store the minimum amount required for a trip into the Wilderness (in addition to the 1,000 ether required to activate the weapon). This mechanic is not indicated on the [[Items Kept on Death]] interface.

==Maximum hit==	
The [[Maximum Magic hit|maximum hit]] dealt by the sceptre is dependent on the player's current visible [[Magic]] level. The formula is as follows:

<math>\begin{align}
\text{Max Hit} &= \lfloor \frac{\text{Magic}}{3} \rfloor - 8\\
\end{align}</math>

